WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest
is an Emmy-nominated write

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.670
and comedian whose work you know
from "Saturday Night Live,

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:07.140
and her comedy special,
"Sam Jay: Three in the Morning."

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
Her new late-night series,
"Pause with Sam Jay"

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
premieres May 21st
on HBO and HBO Max.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:13.613 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:17.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If you really want to help me
just make the laws better.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:18.718 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Cheers to that [bleep]

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:21.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
They've established
a rule of white society.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They want Aunt Jemima
off the syrup.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't even
know the narrative!

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:28.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought Uncle Ben
was a rice tycoon.

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:30.530 line:92%
I was proud to buy that rice

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.131 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:34.768
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend Sam Jay.

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.506 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What's up?

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:40.306 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It's good to see you.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:42.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good to see you.
Welcome, welcome!

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:43.643 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-This is cool.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:46.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We've got a couch for you
and everything.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.948 size:84% position:42%
-It is nice to have you
back in the building.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
You worked here
for "SNL" for three years.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:54.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I imagine,
which I want to talk about

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:56.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
your talk show,
has its own set of stresses.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:58.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you come back, though
in the "SNL" building

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the "SNL" floor,
do you miss it?

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel those old
stress tickles?

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:03.730 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-A little bit.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was walking down the hallway
like, "Oh, this is nice."

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.067 size:78% position:39%
But then I remembered
it's Tuesday night,

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:10.637
and I was like, "I'm so glad
I don't have to deal with this."

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm so glad I'm here
in this capacity.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause you're putting togethe
your own show.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I imagine
one of the first things --

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:18.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the coolest things
is staffing it.

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:19.379 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Did you know right away

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:20.847
the kind of people
you wanted working on your show?

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:23.450
Were they people you'd known
through your life as a stand-up?

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. A lot of stand-ups
on the show.

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:27.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
I knew for sure I wanted peopl
that I would argue with

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:31.291
and who are good at screamin
loudly when they're drunk.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
I need those two things.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you had people like tha
in your life.

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. I had them
immediately ready.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:37.597 size:78% position:39% line:92%
If you're a stand-up,

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think you got those people
on speed-dial.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:42.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And there does seem to be
the element of the show

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
is there's --
exactly what you just said

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is this sort of
party atmosphere

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:48.908 line:92%
and this debate atmosphere

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you been someone
who has enjoyed

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:54.247
being argumentative with friends
over your life?

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
I think my whole life,

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.884 line:92%
I've always liked to argue

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
My family thought
I was going to be a lawyer

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause they were like,
"Oh, 'cause you love to argue,

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:03.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
which, there's way more
to being a lawyer than that.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:06.626
But ever since I was a kid
I was big into arguing, debating

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know, kind of pokin
the bear a little bit.

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:11.197 line:92%
-So, you have this talk show

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
You get this offer
to put it together.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:16.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you sort of decide on,
from that clip,

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
you put it in this party.

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:20.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's got this really nice
verite feel to it.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:25.345
How did you come
and land on that as your format?

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:28.181
-Well, I mean, I don't know.
I just felt like, you know

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, you got the desk
locked down.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what I mean?
-Like, fully. It's got --

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:33.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you know,
God of the desk.

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:35.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was, like, "Hey,
let me try something else

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:36.656 size:78% position:39% line:92%
that I haven't seen."

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:40.560
And also, I just felt like I'm
better in that type of a space

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.695 size:88% position:44%
-When you're doing it,
and obviously, you know,

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're out there
and you're performing,

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're not necessarily
looking directly in the camera

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
the way, you know, I think
conventionally a lot of us d
it.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.471
But you know obviously later
you're going to be in the edit

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you able
to sort of be loose and free

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:56.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
or, as the creator of the show
as the show runner,

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.911
are you also thinking in
your head while you're doing it,

00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:00.346
"Okay, this is working here.
This isn't working there"?

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think I'm thinking
a little bit,

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also being,
like, loose and free.

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:05.885
It's a little bit of a dance
of, like, enjoy the moment

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also, sometimes
I'm, like, directing a camera.

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Go over there,"
you know what I mean?

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:12.058
"It's better over there.
I'm not really saying anything."

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:13.960 size:75% position:38%
So it's a little bit
of doing both jobs.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And is it also about
making all the other peopl

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the room with you
feel comfortable, as well?

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:20.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause you must want them
to have the freedom

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:23.403
to be as loose as they would b
if the cameras weren't there

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:26.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, 100%. That was, like,
super important to me.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:29.209
Like, I was like, "Please don'
be, like, staging my friends

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't move them.
Don't place them."

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:34.547
I didn't want any boom mics,
which drove everybody insane

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:38.751
'cause there's about like 13
individual mics going on at once

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
so the audio
sounds nuts to them.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:43.256
But I just wanted people
to be as comfortable as possible

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:44.958 size:75% position:38%
so they could, like,
truly be themselves.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:47.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'm imagining
the longer you were doing it

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:48.394 line:92%
the more that became the case?

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:52.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. The more you do it,
the more I'm chilling,

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:55.034
and I think if my vibe is chill,
then their vibe is chill.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:58.004
-How has -- I'm assuming,
like a lot of stand-ups,

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.839 line:92%
you've missed it this past year.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:02.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you getting back up
on stages again?

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.710 line:92%
And how has the experience been?

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am.
I'm back up at the Cellar.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:08.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm back up at The Stand,
and it's been great.

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:09.749 line:92%
Like, I miss stand-up so much.

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:13.286
And especially doing this show
it's, like, super stressful,

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:15.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
and weirdly, standing up
in front of strangers

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:18.458
and telling my personal business
is a stress reliever for me.

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it's helped
balance out that energy.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Has it always been
a stress reliever for you?

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:25.098
Because I think for a lot
of people, the idea of,

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially as
an upcoming stand-up

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:27.767 line:92%
in the rooms you mentioned

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
which are pretty famous room
with a lot of big names,

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
when did you cross
that threshold

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:35.208
of stopped being stressed
before you went onstage?

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:38.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um, I don't really know
when it stopped.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.013 line:92%
One day, I just wasn't anymore

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:41.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I think once I realized,

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:42.482 line:92%
like, "I'm going to do this,

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm going to be doing it
for a while."

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:45.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I think
once that lands on you,

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:47.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're like, "Alright,
there's going to be good days,

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:48.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there's going
to be bad days."

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you feel like
audiences are better

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:54.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
for having been
away from live performance

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.728 line:92%
or are they rusty, as well

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:57.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think audiences
are laughing at anything.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's easier
to make them laugh.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:01.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're just so happy to b
outside. You know what I mean?

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:03.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Like, you can say whatever,

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:06.639
and they're, like, dying
laughing and, like, rolled over,

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.708 size:88% position:44%
which is nice, but also,
sometimes, you're like,

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don't know
if that was that funny."

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:11.177 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right. [ Laughs ]

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.212
Well, it's really hard,
because I think, you know, look,

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:15.915
you don't want a dead audience
but you want a true audience

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:18.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially if you're tryin
to build material.

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:20.253 line:92%
And it's really hard sometimes

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:22.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, to have to admit tha
to yourself,

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:25.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
of, "I think literally anythin
would've worked tonight."

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:26.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, but I think,
like, you know,

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:28.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
New Yorkers are,
like, easily jaded.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:30.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, people have been outside
for like a month.

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:31.798 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I think they're over it.

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:36.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I think we'll get
a real New York audience back.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:37.170 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, exactly.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
You started in Boston
doing stand-up,

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:43.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
which has a great stand-up
history, of course.

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you talk about this
in your special.

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:46.279 line:92%
You know, I think less known

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:52.018
for having maybe as divers
a stand-up, you know, scen

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:53.019 size:81% position:41% line:92%
as maybe other places.

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:55.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
As someone who's queer, someon
who's black, as a female,

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:58.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, what was that scene like
for you coming up?

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.093 line:92%
-Ah, very white and very male.

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:02.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Both laugh ]
Like most comedy scenes.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:05.264
But I think, you know, it ha
its times where it was rough

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:08.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I feel it kind of, like,
can be rough to anybody.

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
It didn't feel particular
to me in any way.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.538
But definitely, it can be
a little bit isolating

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:14.707
when you go in a show, and
you're the only Black person

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're the only woman.
You're the only gay person

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:18.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then it's just like
a bunch of, like, white dude

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:20.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
who know all the Red Sox
players. You know what I mean?

00:06:20.413 --> 00:06:23.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're like, "I guess
this is what we're doing."

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.650 line:92%
-Do you feel like, you know,

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.953
after you're a part of the scene
for a while, though,

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:29.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you get up
and you score in enough rooms,

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:31.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
you become part of the team?
-Yeah, for sure.

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:34.861 size:88% position:44%
I think comedy is, like,
a equalizer in that way

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:36.929 size:84% position:42%
where people just need
to see you do it enough

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:37.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be like,
"Oh, she's good at it,"

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:40.833
and then they kind of, like,
just bring you into the fold

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:43.069 size:81% position:41%
-Did you manage to --
I mean, 'cause, again,

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:45.772
part of your show is very much
that talking with comedians.

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:50.309
And I think it's, you know, on
of those elements of stand-u

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:51.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
that people romanticize
all the time

00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:53.980 size:88% position:44%
is how, you know, comics
when they get together,

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
they spend a lot of time
after the show

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:56.682 size:88% position:44% line:92%
hanging out and talking.

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:57.483 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Did you miss that deeply

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:59.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
over this time
that we were all apart?

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:00.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very much.
I think that was part

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:02.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
of what drove me
to make the show the way I did

00:07:02.989 --> 00:07:04.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
was that I missed
hanging out with my friends,

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:06.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I missed arguing
with my friends.

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:08.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was, like,
"Ah, I need this energy

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:09.929 size:78% position:39% line:92%
to happen somewhere."

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:11.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I think that was a littl
bit of, like, I was like,

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:14.567
"Mm, maybe I can get HBO to pa
me to hang out with my friends."

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:15.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Both laugh ]
-That's very smart.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:18.070
Do you tend to -- When you hav
arguments with your friends,

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.972 size:84% position:42%
are you ever convinced
to their point of view?

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:21.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or do you feel like --
-Sometimes.

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:23.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah? Okay, good.
-Sometimes. Not often.

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:24.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm pretty stubborn.
-Right.

00:07:24.477 --> 00:07:26.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think most of the time,
it's agree to disagree.

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:28.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
